  "title": "Daydream Nation",
  "country": "US",
  "released": "1988-10-18",
  "notes": "Allied Record Company (ARC) pressing distinguished by SP-AR and △22278/9 in runouts.  Version without these is [r10302794]. \n\nRecorded and mixed at Greene Street Recording, July/August '88, New York City.\nMastered at Masterdisk, N.Y.C.\nEnigma in association with Blast First.\n- Gatefold jacket.  \n- Includes folded poster (23.5 x 11.5 in.) with a B&W photo of the band by Michael Lavine, dated August 1988.\n- Jacket and poster Printed in Canada.\n- Plain generic white insert sleeves.\n\nLacquers cut with SP in matrix number for pressing at Specialty but then sent to Allied, which subcontracted the plating to Sheffield Lab Matrix.",
  "released_formatted": "18 Oct 1988",
